    "main_topic": [
      {
        "h_title": "Our recommended areas of Chiang Rai to stay in",
        "main_title": "Where to stay in Chiang Rai",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Select which area you’re interested in to browse Travelfish’s recommended hotels, guesthouses, and other places to stay in that area of Chiang Rai.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Chiang Rai",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Chiang Rai",
        "main_title": "Where to stay in Chiang Rai",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 2,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Chiang Rai has some very good choices in all price ranges with a particularly fine selection of budget and flash-packer options. There is a concentration of budget spots on and around Jedyod Road and a great series of mid-range options on Jedyod’s prolongation, Soi Sunpanad. There are also a couple of large hotels—Wiang Inn and Wangcome—down Phaholyothin but otherwise guesthouses and hotels are rather randomly scattered across town so it is useful to have an idea of exactly where you’re going before you arrive. No doubt to encourage visitors to stay longer many places offer bicycle and motorbike hire and provide maps and information and unless you are in a desperate hurry, we would recommend allowing at least two or three nights in the city.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": null,
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Baan Bua Guest House",
        "main_title": "Where to stay in Chiang Rai",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "The simple and unpretentious Baan Bua Guest House is set right at the end of the same alleyway leading off Jetyod as the popular Orchids. A stone’s throw, but world away, from the hustle and bustle of bar street and with a delightful little garden and virtually no traffic noise, at Baan Bua you could be right out in the country rather than a busy city centre. As you emerge into their yard,... Read our full review of Baan Bua Guest House including room rates and direct contact details.",
            "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/accommodation_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/chiang_rai/chiang_rai/all/8797",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/accommodation_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/chiang_rai/chiang_rai/all/8797",
                "anchor_text": "... Read our full review of Baan Bua Guest House including room rates and direct contact details."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Baan Bua Guest House",
            "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/accommodation_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/chiang_rai/chiang_rai/all/8797",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/accommodation_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/chiang_rai/chiang_rai/all/8797",
                "anchor_text": "Baan Bua Guest House"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Baan Baramee",
        "main_title": "Where to stay in Chiang Rai",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Tucked down Soi Sunpanad, off Phaholyothin Road, but hard to miss with a vivid green paint job, is the cute and homely Baan Baramee. With a convivial atmosphere and friendly staff plus a cosy downstairs seating area, it’s a welcoming little spot. Behind the small cafe, where complimentary breakfast is served, and the information and reception desk is a two-storey block with a... Read our full review of Baan Baramee including room rates and direct contact details.",
            "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/accommodation_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/chiang_rai/chiang_rai/all/7330",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/accommodation_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/chiang_rai/chiang_rai/all/7330",
                "anchor_text": "... Read our full review of Baan Baramee including room rates and direct contact details."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Baan Baramee",
            "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/accommodation_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/chiang_rai/chiang_rai/all/7330",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/accommodation_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/chiang_rai/chiang_rai/all/7330",
                "anchor_text": "Baan Baramee"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Baan Jaru",
        "main_title": "Where to stay in Chiang Rai",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Cute little Baan Jaru on the southern stretch of Jetyod Road is a perfect example of a very popular boutique-style guesthouse that comes with a greater reputation than it does capacity.\nSmug, albeit friendly, owners turned us away a couple of times during low season before we actually managed to get a look at their rooms. Their success isn’t rocket science and frankly interiors—apart from... Read our full review of Baan Jaru including room rates and direct contact details.",
            "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/accommodation_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/chiang_rai/chiang_rai/all/8798",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/accommodation_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/chiang_rai/chiang_rai/all/8798",
                "anchor_text": "... Read our full review of Baan Jaru including room rates and direct contact details."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "secondary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Baan Jaru",
            "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/accommodation_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/chiang_rai/chiang_rai/all/8798",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/accommodation_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/chiang_rai/chiang_rai/all/8798",
                "anchor_text": "Baan Jaru"
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "table_content": null
      },
      {
        "h_title": "Baan Soontree Resort",
        "main_title": "Where to stay in Chiang Rai",
        "author": null,
        "language": "en",
        "level": 3,
        "primary_content": [
          {
            "text": "Located on a narrow lane in an extensive residential area to the east of Highway 1, Baan Soontree is a good option for flashpackers and families seeking a small, resort-type place with a pool and willing to forgo a downtown address. The location will be a turn off for some—a solid two kilometres east of the night market and bus station—and if you don’t have your own transport be... Read our full review of Baan Soontree Resort including room rates and direct contact details.",
            "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/accommodation_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/chiang_rai/chiang_rai/all/7547",
            "urls": [
              {
                "url": "https://www.travelfish.org/accommodation_profile/thailand/northern_thailand/chiang_rai/chiang_rai/all/7547",
                "anchor_text": "... Read our full review of Baan Soontree Resort including room rates and direct contact details."
